/E (This carbon intensity number depends primarily on the source of the energy \(like whether the energy was produced from coal or wind or solar sources\) but also things like  - conversion efficiency \(technology to convert into power can be more or less efficient\) - transmission efficiency \(in electricity travelling through power lines\) - incidental/indirect emissions \(such as costs to built the power plants for even a "zero-carbon" energy source\))
